# oracle: fix ilves on a branched molecule (centre atom 1 bonded to 2, 3 and 4; the angle 2-1-3 constrained by the a selector, so one bond-and-angle network of four constraints): angle_style harmonic 109.47 degrees, tol 1e-4 iter 25, thermo and every per-atom position, velocity and force after 50 steps
# oracle-inputs: w50il_branched.data
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-7 abs=1e-9
units           real
atom_style      angle
read_data       w50il_branched.data
pair_style      lj/cut 3.0
pair_coeff      * * 0.05 0.8
bond_style      harmonic
bond_coeff      1 100.0 1.0
angle_style     harmonic
angle_coeff     1 50.0 109.47
special_bonds   lj 1.0 1.0 1.0
neighbor        0.3 bin
timestep        1.0
fix             1 all nve
fix             cons all ilves 1.0e-4 25 0 b 1 a 1
thermo_style    custom step pe ebond eangle press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          10
run             50
